Subject: Cantor SJS Compiled Lookahead Term Set Optimization P0 Justification

@ [justification_uuid] c6e11288-4fb7-408b-9487-6cbb1de44d66
@ [canonical_uuid] 5bb132b9-8250-4f6d-a7e6-6977edad8162

& [Need]
  + compiled stitches need a reproducible way to choose a small source-bound vocabulary without allowing a score to hide governing obligations or launder semantic guesses

& [Decision]
  + use exhaustive bounded selection over supplied typed candidates and an exact lexicographic objective with mandatory coverage and full rejected uncovered accounting

& [WhyNow]
  + the provider-free stitch compiler is published so selecting its future structured terms is the next dependency-contiguous seam

& [Limit]
  + this establishes exact-pool optimization mechanics only; usefulness and acceleration require separately controlled model-specific evidence
